# ECVRF, RFC 9381 section 5.3: the DLEQ proof that Gamma was computed
# with the same key that produced the public key Y.  The verifier's
# U and V equations, written as the relation they check.
#
# H is not a fixed base: it is encode_to_curve(salt, alpha), so it
# moves with the VRF input.  It cannot be the identity -- the curve
# encodings the ciphersuites use have no representation for it -- and
# the verifier separately runs ECVRF_validate_key on Y.
secrets x
claims  x
eq  Y       B
eq  Gamma   H
